# Commits whose only effect is formatting or a mechanical rewrite, so `git blame` skips them: one
# full commit hash per line, newest last. `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`
# reads it, and so does GitHub's blame view.
#
# The file is kept even when it lists nothing. A missing file is not a no-op: `git blame` fails
# outright ("could not open object name list") for anyone who has that config set, so an empty file
# is a working file. Add the hash here when a rewrite lands.
